The Buckled Fence Line~
   A fence of pointed stakes, meant to stop cavalry, has been flattened
in three places and stands bent and twisted in the others.  Torn
banner-silk still hangs from one leaning post.  The ash fields lie east;
north a squat stone tower leans against the sky.~
