#3033
The Sunken Breastwork~
   The earthwork here has been cut down to a shallow trench by years of
rain, but the sharpened stakes in front of it still stand in a double
line.  Rusted caltrops lie in the ash between them.  A well and yard
lie west; the breastwork runs on north.~
